  <!-- ================= STACK ================= -->
  <section class="block" id="stack">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <div>
          <span class="sec-tag">01 — Stack</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title" data-i18n="stack-title">What I build with</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sec-note" data-i18n="stack-note">This is my usual stack, grouped by the part of the system where it works — not a limit. If a project calls for a different stack or a new tool, I can do it: I adapt, learn whatever is needed, and always work following good practices.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="skills">
        <div class="skill-card reveal">
          <span class="card-tag">Frontend</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="sk1-title">The interface</h3>
          <p data-i18n="sk1-desc">What the user sees and touches: structure, behaviour and interactive web applications.</p>
          <ul class="tech-list">
            <li>HTML <span data-i18n="t-html">structure and semantics</span></li>
            <li>CSS <span data-i18n="t-css">styling and visual design</span></li>
            <li>JavaScript <span data-i18n="t-js">logic in the browser</span></li>
            <li>Vue <span data-i18n="t-vue">components and reactivity</span></li>
            <li>Bootstrap <span data-i18n="t-bootstrap">components and responsive grid</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card reveal">
          <span class="card-tag" data-i18n="sk2-tag">Backend · Languages</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="sk2-title">The logic</h3>
          <p data-i18n="sk2-desc">The code that processes, calculates and responds behind the interface, and the databases where the information is stored.</p>
          <ul class="tech-list">
            <li>Node.js <span data-i18n="t-node">JavaScript on the server</span></li>
            <li>Ruby <span data-i18n="t-ruby">scripts and applications</span></li>
            <li>JavaScript <span data-i18n="t-js2">full-stack, also outside the browser</span></li>
            <li>PostgreSQL <span data-i18n="t-pg">relational database</span></li>
            <li>MySQL <span data-i18n="t-mysql">relational database</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card reveal">
          <span class="card-tag" data-i18n="sk3-tag">Infrastructure · DevOps</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="sk3-title">The environment</h3>
          <p data-i18n="sk3-desc">Where the code lives: servers, automated deployments and scheduled tasks.</p>
          <ul class="tech-list">
            <li>Linux <span data-i18n="t-linux">my working system</span></li>
            <li>AWS <span data-i18n="t-aws">cloud and deployment</span></li>
            <li>Docker <span data-i18n="t-docker">containers for development & deployment</span></li>
            <li>Pipelines CI/CD <span data-i18n="t-cicd">continuous integration & delivery</span></li>
            <li>Crontab <span data-i18n="t-cron">automated tasks</span></li>
            <li>Git <span data-i18n="t-git">version control</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="skill-card skills-extra reveal">
        <span class="card-tag" data-i18n="ex-tag">Collaboration · Tools · Extras</span>
        <h3 data-i18n="ex-title">The rest of my toolbox</h3>
        <div class="extra-grid">
          <div class="extra-item"><b>Slack</b><span data-i18n="t-slack">day-to-day team communication</span></div>
          <div class="extra-item"><b>Jira</b><span data-i18n="t-jira">task and project management</span></div>
          <div class="extra-item"><b>Postman</b><span data-i18n="t-postman">testing APIs and endpoints</span></div>
          <div class="extra-item"><b>VS Code</b><span data-i18n="t-vscode">my code editor</span></div>
          <div class="extra-item"><b>Cursor</b><span data-i18n="t-cursor">AI-powered code editor</span></div>
          <div class="extra-item"><b>Copilot · ChatGPT</b><span data-i18n="t-ia">AI assistants I use while coding</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= AVAILABILITY ================= -->
  <section class="block" id="availability">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <div>
          <span class="sec-tag" data-i18n="avail-tag">02 — Availability</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title" data-i18n="avail-title">Open to any format</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sec-note" data-i18n="avail-note">I'm based in Mérida, Yucatán and I'm open to all three ways of working. Pick the one that fits what you need.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="avail-grid">
        <div class="avail-card reveal">
          <div class="avail-num">01</div>
          <span class="card-tag" data-i18n="av1-tag">Employment</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="av1-title">A role on your team</h3>
          <p data-i18n="av1-desc">Join a team as a full-stack developer, covering interface, logic, server and deployment day to day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="avail-card reveal">
          <div class="avail-num">02</div>
          <span class="card-tag">Freelance</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="av2-title">Work by project</h3>
          <p data-i18n="av2-desc">Collaborate as a freelancer on a specific application or system, end to end or on the part you're missing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="avail-card reveal">
          <div class="avail-num">03</div>
          <span class="card-tag" data-i18n="av3-tag">Commissioned</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="av3-title">Commissioned projects</h3>
          <p data-i18n="av3-desc">Build something custom to order: you define it, I build it and leave it running, versioned and deployed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= PROCESS ================= -->
  <section class="block" id="process">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <div>
          <span class="sec-tag" data-i18n="proc-tag">03 — Process</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title" data-i18n="proc-title">How I work</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sec-note" data-i18n="proc-note">Being full-stack means not dropping the problem halfway: I cover every phase with the tools in my stack.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process">
        <div class="step reveal"><span class="n">01</span><h3 data-i18n="p1-title">Understand the problem</h3><p data-i18n="p1-desc">Before writing code: what's needed, who will use it, and which part is interface, which part is logic and which part is server.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><span class="n">02</span><h3 data-i18n="p2-title">Build the interface</h3><p data-i18n="p2-desc">Semantic HTML, CSS and clear JavaScript, with Bootstrap for components and Vue when the application calls for reactive state.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><span class="n">03</span><h3 data-i18n="p3-title">Program the logic</h3><p data-i18n="p3-desc">The backend in Node.js or Ruby depending on the case, with the data in PostgreSQL or MySQL, written so the code stays readable and maintainable later.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><span class="n">04</span><h3 data-i18n="p4-title">Deploy and automate</h3><p data-i18n="p4-desc">Everything versioned with Git, running on Linux and AWS, with Docker, CI/CD pipelines and crontab for anything that repeats on its own.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= PRINCIPLES + CTA ================= -->
  <section class="block" id="principles">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <div>
          <span class="sec-tag" data-i18n="prin-tag">04 — Principles</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title" data-i18n="prin-title">Three rules I don't negotiate</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="principles">
        <div class="principle reveal"><div class="big" data-i18n="pr1-big">If you can't read it,<br />it doesn't work.</div><p data-i18n="pr1-p">Neither the interface nor the code: legible text on screen and code another developer — or me in six months — can understand without a fight.</p></div>
        <div class="principle reveal"><div class="big" data-i18n="pr2-big">Everything versioned,<br />everything in Git.</div><p data-i18n="pr2-p">Every change is recorded. If something breaks, you know what changed, when and why, and you can roll it back.</p></div>
        <div class="principle reveal"><div class="big" data-i18n="pr3-big">Anything repetitive<br />gets automated.</div><p data-i18n="pr3-p">That's what CI/CD pipelines and crontab are for: what a machine can do on its own shouldn't be done by a person by hand.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta reveal" id="contact">
        <div class="ring" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <span class="sec-tag" data-i18n="cta-tag">05 — Let's talk</span>
        <h2 data-i18n="cta-title">Need a <span class="hl">full-stack</span> developer on your team?</h2>
        <p data-i18n="cta-p">I'm open to employment, freelance work and commissioned projects where you need someone who covers the full cycle: interface, logic, server and deployment. Reach me by email or LinkedIn — I reply on either.</p>
        <div class="contact-grid">
          <a class="contact-item" href="mailto:rusell_may@outlook.com">
            <small data-i18n="c-email-label">Email</small>
            <strong>rusell_may@outlook.com</strong>
            <span class="sub" data-i18n="c-email-sub">Write to me directly →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="contact-item" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rusell-may" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <small>LinkedIn</small>
            <strong>linkedin.com/in/rusell-may</strong>
            <span class="sub" data-i18n="c-linkedin-sub">Connect or send me a message →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="contact-item" href="https://github.com/rusellmay" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <small>GitHub</small>
            <strong>github.com/rusellmay</strong>
            <span class="sub" data-i18n="c-github-sub">My code and repositories →</span>
          </a>
          <div class="contact-item">
            <small data-i18n="c-loc-label">Location</small>
            <strong>Mérida, Yucatán</strong>
            <span class="sub" data-i18n="c-loc-sub">Mexico · open to remote work</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-accent magnetic" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rusell-may" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-i18n="cta-btn-linkedin">Go to my LinkedIn</span> <span class="arr">↗</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost magnetic" href="mailto:rusell_may@outlook.com"><span data-i18n="cta-btn-email">Email me</span> <span class="arr">↗</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost magnetic" href="https://github.com/rusellmay" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub <span class="arr">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

